<!--
    maxlinewidth and commentindent: the console line-size options.

    Ported from decompiler/cpp/options.cc (OptionMaxLineWidth,
    OptionCommentIndent), printlanguage.cc (setLineCommentIndent) and
    prettyprint.cc (EmitPrettyPrint). Upstream prints through EmitPrettyPrint,
    which breaks lines longer than maxlinewidth. kuna printed through the
    plain emitter only, so `option maxlinewidth` was accepted and did nothing.

    Stage P9 (emit). The default stays one line per statement; setting
    maxlinewidth routes the plain text through the pretty printer.

    Authored x86-64 (nasm): f returns the sum of five products of its six
    arguments.

    Pass 1 (default): the prototype and the return are each one line.
    Pass 2 (`option maxlinewidth 40`): both break at 40 columns.

-->
